SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE — it does NOT cover the mirrored documentation.

The MIT grant above applies only to the original material written for this
repository: the 14 `SKILL.md` guides, the Python helpers under
`pyrate-command-reference/scripts/` and `pyrate-input-file/scripts/`, the
acceptance gates under `scripts/`, the fixture index
`assets/files/README.md`, `README.md`, `.gitignore` and the repository
organisation.

EXCEPTION — everything under any `references/` directory is a verbatim local
mirror of the PyRate documentation (the GitHub wiki at
<https://github.com/dsilvestro/PyRate/wiki> and the `tutorials/` pages at
<https://github.com/dsilvestro/PyRate/tree/master/tutorials>), which is part of
PyRate, authored by D. Silvestro and collaborators and licensed **AGPLv3**
(see <https://github.com/dsilvestro/PyRate>, "PyRate is licensed under a AGPLv3
License", mirrored verbatim at `pyrate/references/home.md:24` = corpus
`PyRate-wiki/Home.md:16`). The only
changes made to a mirror are a YAML frontmatter block recording its
`source_url`/`mirrored_from` and the re-pointing of image paths to
`../../assets/images/`. This file does not re-license those mirrors, grants you
nothing beyond what the upstream AGPLv3 already allows, and does not waive the
upstream authors' rights.

The same holds for the images under `assets/images/`: they are byte-for-byte
copies of figures shipped with the upstream documentation and remain under
upstream terms.

One further exception, stated for the avoidance of doubt: the 25 `*-cn.md`
files under `references/` are NOT upstream pages. They are local
Simplified-Chinese translations produced in the workspace that assembled this
suite (they are untracked in both upstream checkouts); they translate the
AGPLv3 upstream English pages and are therefore derivative works of that
documentation, not MIT-licensed original material of this repository.

Fixtures under `assets/files/` are transcriptions or reformattings of code
blocks and tables printed by the mirrored documentation, plus worked examples
this suite constructed where the documentation prints no data; each file's own
provenance header, and `assets/files/README.md`, states which is which. Where a
fixture reproduces upstream text or data, upstream terms apply to that span.

See `LICENSE.md` for the corpus, the git revisions the mirrors were taken from,
and the warranty disclaimer.
